# Implementation Plan - Add Clear All Button to Settings

Adding a "Danger Zone" section to the Settings page for administrative tasks, specifically for clearing all medicine data.

## Proposed Changes

### [Frontend] Settings Page UI
Add a new section to the settings dashboard for administrative actions.

#### [MODIFY] [data-import-settings.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/settings/data-import-settings.tsx) or [page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/settings/page.tsx)
- Add a "Danger Zone" card containing the "Clear All Medicines" button.
- Ensure the section is only visible or enabled for users with the `ADMIN` role.
- Implement a confirmation dialog (e.g., using a Shadcn Dialog or a simple `window.confirm`) to prevent accidental deletions.
- On confirmation, call `DELETE /api/medicines/clear-all`.
- Show success/error toasts.

### [API] Access Control Verification
Verify that the `DELETE /api/medicines/clear-all` endpoint itself correctly enforces the `ADMIN` role. (Already implemented in previous steps, but will double-check).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build`.

### Manual Verification
- Log in as a `MANAGER` or `CASHIER` and verify the button is hidden or disabled.
- Log in as an `ADMIN` and verify the button is visible.
- Click the button and ensure the confirmation dialog appears.
- Confirm the deletion and verify the medicines list is emptied.
